    "body": "## Problem\r\nIn the Nvim documentation, there's a section  ([link](https://neovim.io/doc/user/nvim/#_what-now%3f)) on customization via config files which uses two fragments to allow deep-linking into a code snippet. One of them (config-example) is redundant, with no additional references anywhere else in the codebase. The other one (example-init) correctly leads navigation toward the snippet while also being used as a reference further down in the documentation.\r\n\r\nI tracked the addition of this string to [this PR](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/a3b48b1054d01084face54d830f35c7a5a4e35a4#diff-fb4f379621ac3eedf519a290742d7fcb5d9b145f5ea61e71b50b4699f1394583R28)\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nRemoval of the *config-example* string.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-19T09:37:22Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> with no additional references anywhere else in the codebase.\r\n\r\ntags exist for `:h foo<tab>` completion/discovery as well. I added `config-example` because `config` is the common name for init.lua/init.vim/vimrc/... related topics.\r\n\r\nI don't understand the other part of your problem statement... what is the problem being solved here?",
            "created_at": "2026-09-19T08:04:36Z",
