            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Fair. I didn't consider the tag completion to an alternative name as I was going through the tutorial online. It felt strange having a fragment that pointed to the same snippet side by side to another one that meant essentially the same (like in the screenshot). My bad! Should've researched more 🥲\r\n\r\nI'll close the PR since there's no problem to be solved \r\n\r\n<img width=\"787\" height=\"564\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-19 at 06 19 58\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29c2adfb-d2a6-44fe-8ddd-dd38e499dca4\" />",
